services:
  trader:
    command:
      - -m
      - scripts.run_live
      - --trade-args
      - --loop
      - --cycle-seconds
      - "60"
      - --mode
      - live
      - --place-orders
      - --compound
      - --bankroll
      - "500"
      - --max-stake-dollars
      - "40"
      # **0.5, not 1.5, because a maker pays a different toll.** 1.5pp was
      # sized for a TAKER: the fee averages ~1.1pp of stake plus a 0.5c
      # half-spread, so ~1.6pp had to be cleared before a crossing trade paid.
      # Resting at the bid costs nothing and buys at a full cent better, so the
      # cost is a CREDIT of ~0.465pp against the mid, not a charge — measured
      # 2026-10-18, net +1.382pp at t=+5.17 with 100% of rows tradeable.
      # At 1.5pp the model placed no orders at all and collected no fill data,
      # which is the one thing maker entry was switched on to gather.
      # Must match the `retrain` service, or the gates grade a policy the
      # account does not run.
      - --min-edge-pp
      - "0.5"
      - --kelly-fraction
      - "0.10"
      - --entry-offsets
      - "3"
      - "6"
      - "9"
      - "12"
      - --require-peer-book
      # A hole in the middle of the book. The fee 0.07*p(1-p) peaks at a coin
      # flip -- 1.75pp of stake against 0.33pp at 95c -- and the measured signal
      # there is ~0: on live-recorded quotes the 35-65c band alone lost $393
      # (-2.38pp/ct) while excluding it took the whole book from -$55 to +$297.
      # **Must stay identical to the `retrain` service's own flag**, or the
      # gates score a policy the account does not run -- which is exactly the
      # drift found on 2026-10-18, where the retrain graded wait_12 at 0.05
      # Kelly while this traded first-clear across four offsets at 0.10.
      - --exclude-price-band
      - "0.35,0.65"
      # **Rest at the bid instead of lifting the ask.** The venue charges makers
      # nothing and the entry is a full cent better on a measured 1.000c spread
      # -- together ~1.5-2pp per contract, against a model edge of ~1.1-1.5pp,
      # so the execution cost had been larger than the entire signal. Measured
      # 2026-10-18 on 54,100 live-recorded rows, the SAME model with no
      # retraining: -$77.25 taker against +$2,445.76 maker.
      #
      # **This is a live EXPERIMENT, not a validated setting.** All 1,556 fills
      # on this account are `is_taker: true` -- no resting order has ever filled
      # here, and the backtest assumes every one does. The likeliest outcome is
      # simply fewer fills: one observed book had 441 contracts already queued
      # at the bid and we join behind them. A session with zero fills is a
      # RESULT, not a fault. The gates are scored at the ask on purpose, so
      # they bound this from below rather than banking the assumption.
      - --maker-entry
      # Pull an unfilled order after 60s of its OWN age. The forecast is what
      # expires -- `sigma_remaining` is computed for the decision instant -- so
      # a fill arriving minutes later takes an edge that has already moved.
      - --maker-cancel-seconds
      - "60"
      - --no-require-gates
      - --force
      - --reason
      - "live forward test; gates fail on the market comparison (model_minus_market, model_minus_market_p, calibration_vs_market) and the operator authorised real orders. --require-model-version was REMOVED 2026-10-18, so this no longer names one artifact - whatever the Sunday retrain installs trades at the next window boundary, unreviewed."
